  "narrative": {
    "summaryIntro": "Jagannath Temple in Puri, Odisha, is one of the four cardinal pilgrimage sites (Char Dham) and ranks among the most important temples in Hinduism. The temple is dedicated to Jagannath (a form of Krishna) along with his siblings Balabhadra (Balarama) and Subhadra. The main spire stands at a height of approximately 65.76 meters and dominates the Puri skyline.\n\nThe temple is renowned for its annual Rath Yatra (Chariot Festival), one of the most spectacular religious processions in the world, where millions of devotees gather to witness the deities being pulled through the streets in massive wooden chariots. The temple's rich traditions and architectural magnificence make it a UNESCO World Heritage Site and a major spiritual center.",
